{"name":"Osprey","hex":"#63564b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Osprey","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Sarasota County, Florida, United States.","A model of tiltrotor aircraft used especially by naval infantry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Osprey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Osprey","blocks":[{"text":"The osprey, historically known as sea hawk, river hawk, and fish hawk, is a diurnal, fish-eating bird of prey with a cosmopolitan range. It is a large raptor, reaching more than 60 cm (24 in) in length and a wingspan of 180 cm (71 in). It is brown on the upperparts and predominantly greyish on the head and underparts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Osprey_Perched_Snag_Heislerville.jpg/330px-Osprey_Perched_Snag_Heislerville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osprey","wikidata":"Q25332"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Pandion_haliaetus_%28Nagarhole%2C_2010%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Pandion_haliaetus_%28Nagarhole%2C_2010%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Pandion_haliaetus_%28Nagarhole%2C_2010%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Pandion_haliaetus_%28Nagarhole%2C_2010%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Pandion_haliaetus_%28Nagarhole%2C_2010%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Pandion_haliaetus_%28Nagarhole%2C_2010%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APandion_haliaetus_(Nagarhole%2C_2010)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Osprey_mg_9605_%28cropped%2